Greetings,

I hope you're doing well.

Last Friday Thorwin agents came to my suite to identify a solution for the =
upcoming removal of laundry services and storage facilities with the goal o=
f installing en suite laundry machines.

It has been 129 days since my previous email to you regarding this issue an=
d I have not received any clarity on what your plan is.

The electrical system in my suite is from the 1950s, there is no storage sp=
ace for a washer/dryer in the suite, and if there were some space with whic=
h to place the units it would require opening up the floor boards and exten=
ding the pipes.

My understanding is that Thorwin has full intention of removing the storage=
 and laundry services, which I have paid for in my entire residency here, f=
orcing a renovation on me that will negatively affect my quality of living =
through the day to day work, reducing my storage space capabilities, and of=
 course, increasing the rent far above what it should be if provincial guid=
elines were followed in good faith.

I want to be clear that I do not want en suite laundry services and I do no=
t want my storage space removed.

I look forward to hearing your solutions.

Thank you,
Evan Rosner
10-585 Corydon Ave




